1
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Twelve is the new eleven.

2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Ocean's Twelve is a thriller, crime film directed by Steven Soderbergh.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Despite pulling off one of the biggest heists in Las Vegas history and splitting the $160 million take, each
of the infamous Ocean's crew have tried to go straight, lay low and live a legit life ...

4
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
but that's proven to be a challenge.

5
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Casino owner Terry Benedict demands that Danny Ocean return
the money, plus millions more in interest.

6
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Unable to come up the cash, the crew is forced to come together to pull off another series of heists,
this time in Rome, Paris, and Amsterdam – but a Europol agent is hot on their heels.

7
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Danny Ocean, played by George Clooney.

8
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Tess Ocean, played by Julia Roberts.

9
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Rusty Ryan, played by Brad Pitt.

10
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Linus Caldwell, played by Matt Damon.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Isabel Lahiri, played by Catherine Zeta-Jones.

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Terry Benedict, played by Andy Garcia.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
Ocean's Twelve is a 2004 American heist comedy film directed by
Steven Soderbergh and written by George Nolfi.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The second installment in the Ocean's film trilogy franchise and the sequel to Ocean's Eleven (2001), the film features an ensemble cast including George Clooney, Brad Pitt, Matt
Damon, Catherine Zeta-Jones, Andy García, Don Cheadle, Bernie Mac, Julia Roberts, Casey Affleck, Scott Caan, Vincent Cassel, Eddie Jemison, Carl Reiner, and Elliott Gould.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
Ocean's Twelve was released theatrically in the United
States on December 10, 2004, by Warner Bros.

16
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $362.9 million
worldwide, becoming the tenth-highest-grossing film of 2004.

17
01:46:15,000 --> 01:46:21,000
It was followed by Ocean's Thirteen (2007), with
Soderbergh and most of the cast again returning.

18
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The film explores themes of paris, france, rome, italy,
amsterdam, netherlands, competition, ex-girlfriend.

19
01:58:45,000 --> 01:58:51,000
The tone is intense.
